      "claim": "The Population Regression Function (PRF) represents the true, unknown conditional expectation of Y given X in the entire population.",
      "evidence": "Standard econometric definition: PRF = E(Y|X). It is a theoretical construct describing the underlying data-generating process.",
      "weight": 0.3
